data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\", \"content\": \"# Reply to d002: implement greet(name), tested\\n\\nAll three criteria are met.\\n\\n1. **`src/greet.py`** — created. Defines `greet(name)` returning\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` → `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. **`tests/test_greet.py`** — created. Uses `unittest`, covers:\\n   - normal name: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - empty string: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n3. **Verification** — run from the repo root:\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: 0 (all tests pass).\\n\\n**Commit:** `1928a68 Implement greet(name) with unittest tests (d002)` on branch\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` (files: `src/greet.py`,\\n`tests/test_greet.py` — nothing else added or changed).\\n\"}","name":"write"},"id":"call_4ae02432e957412884d897ee","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793607246,"id":"chatcmpl-d16620d518f345cf80e6d4554742b6f2","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

